(in-progress:)

2026-08-05 (v0.0.4)
  * The web server has been removed (an SSH server may replace it)
  * 32-bit builds charged the wrong region maintenance above 235 regions, often
    a negative amount, and misspent a computer baron's gold above 43 million
  * Windows: console ANSI handling is enabled automatically, and the
    Configuration Editor falls back to plain text on the legacy console, so
    "-reset" no longer needs the "ForceV2" registry setting (#98)
  * config-during-reset: a day is 10 turns by default; a new realm gets 15
    turns of protection
  * Worlds saved before v0.0.3 load again, with their mail text preserved
  * "-reset" works on a world the game can no longer read
  * A door caller whose BBS reports no ANSI support is sent plain text (#101)
  * Added "-no-ansi" to send plain text on a terminal that could render it
  * Added "-ascii" for a terminal that reads neither CP437 nor UTF-8
  * The game can be installed with Homebrew on macOS and Linux
  * Sysops: "-gen-coord-key" and "-coord-key" set up the league coordinator
    key; "-league-reset DATE" starts a new season on every board (#65)
  * The league Coordinator sends the roster of boards to every board (#64)
  * A board in a league has no computer barons, and none can be added
  * League orders carry the coordinator's signature, and a board refuses any
    it cannot check (#53)
  * A packet that arrives twice is ignored (#53)
  * The Configuration Editor gained the interplanetary settings: per-day caps
    for group attacks, terrorist ops and bombing ops, attack and terrorism
    costs, switches for bombing, missile and Doomer Kaboomer operations, and
    how long a strike waits for a result before its forces come home
  * The line-based Configuration Editor is split across four pages, moved
    through with N and P (#100)
  * Game Setup shows the whole ruleset
  * Game Setup shows the interplanetary rules on a league board
  * The Doomer Kaboomer is built the way the original builds it: funded a
    million gold at a time, priced by the target planet's size, and launched
    or scrapped by the baron who started it (#16)
  * A planet is warned about a Doomer Kaboomer aimed at it while it is being
    built and while it is in the air, and can send jets to intercept (#63)
  * Implemented Indiv. Attack Force: strike one named baron on another planet
    without waiting for a group to form (#62)
  * Spying on another planet queries that planet and returns real figures (#61)
  * Group attacks, terrorist ops and bombing ops have their own per-day limits
  * Forces sent to another board come home if no result arrives within the
    number of days the game settings allow (#96)
  * Implemented Queen Royale tax refund (#93)
  * A treaty proposer is told whether the offer was accepted or rejected
  * View Treaties lists every realm
  * View Treaties lists sent treaty offers that are still unanswered (#92)
  * A new treaty offer to the same realm replaces the one still waiting
  * Alliance Strength gained a Total Forces line
  * Send Spy succeeds just over half the time, whatever agents either side
    holds
  * Covert agents cost more the longer a realm has been playing
  * Unit prices move within the original's price ranges
  * Debt no longer lowers net worth
  * A dead realm is worth nothing on the scores screen
  * Lists that cannot show a moving highlight are numbered instead, and the
    highlighted row is marked with a character as well as a color (#99)
  * A failed action is marked with a character, so it is not told from a
    successful one by color alone
  * Messages longer than the screen break between words
  * The title screen fits a 24-row terminal, and its prompt sits directly
    below the art
  * New mail is shown at the start of a turn instead of being offered first
  * Enter is ignored at the message prompt
  * Message boxes match the original's size and show the send time
  * "Since your last play" items are numbered and timestamped
  * Treaty offers, View Treaties and Alliance Strength match the original's
    layout and colors
  * Maintenance paid under Auto-Pay is reported as one total, as the original
    reports it
  * The Daily Bulletin title omits the board name on a stand-alone board
  * The System menu lists Covert Operations
  * German and Russian said food had SPOILED where it was consumed

2026-07-31 (v0.0.3)
  * Updating from an earlier version requires a game reset (-reset)
  * Updating also requires running "immortal-barons -set-dropfile" once:
    the door now needs to know which drop file your BBS writes, and will
    not start until it is set
  * PCBOARD.SYS and DORINFO1.DEF drop files are now supported, along
    with DOOR32.SYS and DOOR.SYS
  * Computer barons play far better — they build a mix of region types,
    manufacture their own units, set their tax rate, propose treaties,
    run covert operations, and turn to defense when threatened (#69)
  * Land maintenance now costs what it does in the original — much more
    than before, so holding a large realm is a real expense; military
    maintenance is ten times cheaper, also matching the original
  * Land is no longer unlimited — each realm gets a daily allowance of
    new land it may buy ("Land Created / Day" in the game settings)
  * Technology regions now work as in the original: research builds up
    over many turns across fifteen areas, and selling the regions keeps
    what you have already learned
  * The Queen Royale now takes a tax from each turn's income; paying her
    short costs popular support (#52)
  * Popular support now follows the original's math: a tax rate under
    30% wins support back every turn, and riots cost more the harder you
    tax
  * The gold asked for to boost popular support now grows with your
    population
  * Two empires now hold one agreement at a time, as in the original: a
    new pact replaces the one before it (#88)
  * Declaration Of War ends an agreement with no cost at home; attacking
    a realm you have an agreement with breaks it and costs you popular
    support instead (#88)
  * An ally in a Full Defense Alliance now sends 30% of its mobile
    forces to help defend you
  * A Regular Attack captures more regions from a target whose net worth
    is spread thin over its land, and fewer from a dense, developed one
  * A tank is now worth three troopers with no Headquarters, rising to
    five with a finished one, matching the original — it used to be four
    rising to eight
  * A HeadQuarters costs more the longer your realm has been playing,
    matching the original — build one early
  * Only troopers eat food now, matching the original — jets and tanks
    were being charged for rations they never needed, so an armored
    realm was paying about 40% too much food
  * Rivers now produce gold and food every turn, instead of one or the
    other (#67)
  * Agricultural regions grow a little more food in a good year, instead
    of the same amount every turn, matching the original
  * Desert regions earn more, matching the original game
  * A player attacked while at the menus now sees a notice at their next
    keypress, and attack/sell orders trimmed by concurrent losses say so
  * A realm whose owner never played a turn is removed at the next
    maintenance, and so is any realm left unplayed for 10 days; you can
    always start a new realm afterwards (#83)
  * Maintenance now advances the game at most one day at a time, so the
    computer barons cannot race ahead while nobody is playing
  * Read Messages now shows one message at a time (Reply/Delete/Ignore/
    Quit), matching the original — Ignore keeps a message for next time,
    only Delete removes it
  * The date the game started now appears above the main menu
  * The Queen Royale now makes proclamations in the daily news
  * Sysops: "immortal-barons -spectate N" plays a computer-only game for
    N days and prints a per-day summary, for balance testing (#42)

2026-07-24 (v0.0.2)
  * Winning a Regular Attack now lets you choose the types of the
    regions you capture (#58)
  * Winning a pirate raid that seizes land lets you choose its region
    types too (#21)
  * Combat reports now break down casualties by unit type for both
    the attacker and the defender
  * Pirate raids now happen randomly across turns (about 1 in 5)
    instead of all at once each day (#21)
  * The army now eats far less food, matching the original game — a
    large standing army is no longer food-crippling
  * Renamed the pirate factions to original names
  * Screens follow BRE more closely — highlighted figures, the news
    masthead/bulletin layout, and region-table colors
  * "Since your last play" events now show after you start your turn,
    not before the main menu
  * Windows door: works when the BBS hands over a non-blocking socket
    (MagicBBS) (#37)

2026-07-22
  * v0.0.1 released
